dependency-reduced-pom.xml
node_modules
package-lock.json
# As of task 3.2 the commons module has a build toolchain worth pinning — the ES module
# generator and the Babel presets that decide what the emitted package contains — so its
# resolved versions are committed and the emit is reproducible from a clean clone. Note what
# this lockfile does NOT pin: the package declares no `dependencies`, only peerDependencies and
# devDependencies, so nothing here is resolved on a consumer's behalf. The other ui modules keep
# the blanket ignore until they emit a package of their own.
!commons/package-lock.json
# Task 3.3: user now emits a package too, and runs through the same emitter in ui/build, so its
# resolved toolchain versions are pinned for the same reason. Same caveat as above — this package
# declares no `dependencies`, only peerDependencies and devDependencies, so the lockfile resolves
# nothing on a consumer's behalf. Note it does NOT pin @openidentityplatform/ui-commons: that peer
# is on no registry until task 3.11 and is marked optional so npm can build a tree at all.
!user/package-lock.json
node/
